Reason:  
2result.sql first identifies the 2008 top‑5 minor categories in a CTE (so the logic adapts automatically if the data changes), then calculates yearly totals and percentage shares, and finally pivots the result to one row per year with a clear, compact IF‑based conditional aggregation. The other scripts either hard‑code category names (0result.sql) or duplicate similar logic less concisely (1result.sql). Thus 2result.sql is the correct and simplest solution.